  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Muthulakshmi vs The State Of Tamilnadu on 1 August, 2024 Author: A.D.Jagadish Chandira Bench: A.D.Jagadish Chandira W.P.(Md) No.28300 of 20 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 01.08.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice A.D.Jagadish Chandira and The Honourable Mr.Justice K.Rajasekar W.P.(Md) No.28300 of 2023 and W.M.P.(Md) No.24381 of 2023 Muthulakshmi ... Peti -vs- 1.The State of Tamilnadu rep.by the Home Secretary Government of Tamil Nadu Fort St.George, Chennai 2.The State of Tamilnadu rep.by the Principal Secretary Home (Prison) Department Government of Tamil Nadu Fort St.George, Chennai 3.The Additional Director General of Police / Inspector of Police C.M.D.A. Towers Ii No., Gandhi Irvin Road Egmore, Chennai-8 4.The Deputy Inspector General of Prisons Madurai Circle Madurai _______________ Muthulakshmi vs The State Of Tamilnadu on 1 August, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/94225055/ 1 Page 1 of 12 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.(Md) No.28300 5.The Superintendent of Central Prison Central Prison, Madurai Madurai District 6.The Inspector of Police Y.Othakkadai Police Station Madurai District ... Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of India, a writ of certiorarified mandamus to call for the records connected wit impugned order passed by the first respondent in G.O.(D) No.1188, Home (Prison-IV) Department, dated 16.10.2023, quash the same as illegal and direct the first respondent to release the petitioner's husband, namely son of Muthaiah, L.C.T.No.5201, from the fifth respondent prison, in accordance with G.O.(Ms) No.488, dated 15.11.2021. For Petitioner : Mr.S.Sivaprakash For Respondents : Mr.A.Thiruvadi Kumar Additional Public Prosecutor Order [Order of the Court was made by A.D.JAGADISH CHANDIRA, J.]",
    "facts": "The petitioner has filed this writ petition seeking to quash the impugned order in G.O.(D) No.1188, Home (Prison-IV) Department, dated 16.10.2023, passed by the first respondent and to direct the first respondent _______________ https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis to release her husband, namely, Pandi (L.C.T.No.5201), based on G.O.(Ms) No. 488, dated 15.11.2021, prematurely. 2. It is the case of the petitioner that her husband Pandi (L.C.T.No.5201) is a life convict and he is lodged in the Central Prison. He made a representation to the respondents, seeking premature release based on G.O.(Ms) No.488, Home (Prison-IV) Department, dated 15.11.2021, as he has completed ten years of actual imprisonment as on 15.09.2021. However, the first respondent, by the impugned order dated 16.10.2023, has rejected the plea of the convict, on the ground that he has not served fourteen years of imprisonment.",
    "arguments": "his remission would be premature, since he has not even completed 14 years of sentence in prison."
  },
